    {
      "paragraph_number": 1,
      "text": "The objectives of the SAFFIRE (Spacecraft Fire Experiment) experiments are to (1) determine how rapidly a large scale fire grows in low-gravity and (2) investigate the low-g flammability limits compared to those obtained in NASA’s normal gravity material flammability screening test. The specific objective of SAFFIRE-II tests is to quantify that affect in long-duration low-gravity using samples of the same size as those used in the NASA-STD-6001 Test 1 normal-gravity tests. SAFFIRE-II has a sample card that contains 9 samples, each 5 cm x 29 cm. Sample composition is described in Table 1 and position on the sample card is illustrated in Figure 1.",
      "style": null,
      "figure_table_references": []
    },
    {
      "paragraph_number": 3,
      "text": " Table 1. Saffire-II Samples",
      "style": null,
      "figure_table_references": [
        "Table 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_number": 6,
      "text": "Figure 1. Sample Layout for Saffire-II",
      "style": null,
      "figure_table_references": [
        "Figure 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_number": 9,
      "text": "In addition to the 9 samples, data was also collected for pre-flow and post-flow. These image sets are denoted as F1 for pre-flow and F2 for post-flow.",
      "style": null,
      "figure_table_references": []
    },
    {
      "paragraph_number": 10,
      "text": "The experiment data is organized in PSI by sample number and camera number. There were 2 cameras capturing images during the experiment and they are denoted as C1 for camera 1 and C2 for camera 2. There are various documents and associated information located on the different tabs within the SAFFIRE Investigations records in PSI. A very useful document to review first is the “SAFFIRE Objectives, Development and Status.pdf” document located on the “Overview” tab in the Summary Document section. The experiment records are found on the “Data” tab in the SAFFIRE-II Investigations record. Table 2 contains list of experiment records in PSI and a short description of what each record contains.",
